course: dictionary
lesson: 11008
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Water is a word with several meanings, so the words around it show you which one is meant. «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Air and solids are things, so water here is a thing too: the clear liquid in rivers and lakes.
explain: Water can also be an action word. «To water plants» means to give them water. When you see water next to plants, a garden, or a watering can, you know it means to give a drink.
explain: Some meanings are only found in phrases. «In hot water» means in trouble, not in a warm bath. «Water under the bridge» means something is over and forgiven. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Water means a clear liquid, like the water in rivers, lakes, rain and the sea.
fact: «To water» means to give plants or animals water.
fact: «Waters» can mean a sea or a lake area, as in «the open waters».
fact: To «water something down» means to add water so it is weaker, or to make an idea less strong.
fact: «In hot water» means in trouble, and «water under the bridge» means something is over and forgiven.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» What kind of thing is water here? | *A clear liquid, like the water in rivers and lakes | To give plants a drink | To make something weaker | Tears that come from your eyes
exercise: Jayden's mum says, «You're in hot water now.» What does hot water mean? | Water that is heated for a cup of tea | *In trouble | A very warm bath | Angry at the weather
exercise: Mia says, «My eyes water when I chop onions.» What does water mean here? | *Tears come out of your eyes | To add water to make something weaker | To give plants a drink | A clear liquid in a glass
test: «Baptists and many Pentecostal churches baptise people by full immersion, which means going right under the water.» What does going right under the water mean? | Going to sleep in a boat | Going for a walk on a bridge | Going for a swim in a pool | *Going all the way beneath the surface, fully covered
test: Dad says, «That idea has been watered down now.» What does watered down mean? | *Made weaker and less strong | Given more water to drink | Full of tears | Made sparkly and clean
exam: In a science report, which word is the formal name for water? | Wet | Watering | *H2O | Waters
